("FigS17_depth_by_continent.png", "Depth distribution of soil carbon by continent.", "(A) Ring charts of the share of SOC (outer ring) and SIC (inner ring) in 0 to 30, 30 to 100, and 100 to 200 cm for the globe and six continents; numbers above give the share of each pool below 30 cm and numbers below the total carbon stock (0 to 200 cm). (B) SOC (upper bar) and SIC (lower bar) stocks by depth layer and continent (Pg C); error bars, ±1 SD across the 10 fold-models; the SIC share of total carbon is given at the right. Totals are sums of fold-model mean maps (global 4112 Pg; the Monte Carlo mean in table S5 is 4105 Pg). AS, Asia; EU, Europe; NA, North America; SA, South America; AF, Africa; OC, Oceania. Values in table S13."),
("FigS18_per_GCM_spread.png", "Climate-model and fold-model spread of projected changes.", "Equilibrium change by 2081–2100 in (A) SOC, (B) SIC, and (C) total carbon (0 to 200 cm, Pg C) and (D) area-weighted mean change in topsoil pH, for each of six CMIP6 models under four SSPs. Large symbols, mean across the 10 fold-models for each GCM; small dots (A and B), individual fold-models; vertical lines (C and D), 5th to 95th percentiles across fold-models; black horizontal lines and shaded boxes, ensemble mean and 90% CI across all 60 members (as in table S7). Values in table S16. Each GCM uses a distinct marker shape and high-contrast color (not near-identical greens)."),
("FigS19_SSP_dTC_agreement.png", "Equilibrium change in total soil carbon across scenarios and ensemble agreement.", "(A to D) Equilibrium change in total carbon (ΔTC = ΔSOC + ΔSIC, 0 to 200 cm, Mg C ha⁻¹) by 2081–2100 under SSP1-2.6 (A), SSP2-4.5 (B), SSP3-7.0 (C), and SSP5-8.5 (D) (ensemble means; global sums −45, −79, −114, and −150 Pg). (E and F) Percentage of the 60 ensemble members (10 fold-models × 6 GCMs) with ΔSOC < 0 (E) and ΔSIC > 0 (F) in 0 to 200 cm under SSP5-8.5; cells with an ensemble-mean change smaller than 1 Mg C ha⁻¹ in magnitude are shown separately (|Δ| < 1). Insets give the proportion of land area in each class. Grey, not mapped."),
("FigS20_uncertainty_maps.png", "Spatial uncertainty of present-day stocks.", "Coefficient of variation (CV, %) across the 10 fold-models for (A) SOC in 0 to 200 cm, (B) SIC in 0 to 200 cm, and (C) MAOC in 0 to 30 cm; insets give the proportion of land area in each class. Cells with a mean stock below 0.5 Mg C ha⁻¹ are not shown (grey). (D) Probability density of log₁₀ CV per cell; dashed lines mark medians (SOC 7%, SIC 30%, MAOC 12%). The CV reflects fold-model spread only and excludes the Monte Carlo perturbations used for global totals (fig. S14)."),
("FigS21_koppen_transitions.png", "Köppen–Geiger main-class transitions and associated carbon change under SSP5-8.5.", "(A) Cells that change main class between 1991–2020 and 2071–2099 under SSP5-8.5 [Beck et al.], colored by the seven largest transitions (other transitions pooled; white, no change of main class); the inset gives the share of the shifted area per transition. (B) Area flows (Mkm²) between main classes; pale flows denote unchanged classes. (C) Equilibrium ΔSOC and ΔSIC (0 to 200 cm, Pg C) on land undergoing each transition with an area ≥0.3 Mkm² (bars, ensemble means; error bars, 5th to 95th percentiles of 60 members) and transition area (diamonds, right axis). (D) Total equilibrium ΔSOC (blue) and ΔSIC (purple) on shifted land for four SSPs; numbers give the shifted area (Mkm²) (compare table S8). Values in table S17. Sankey node labels enlarged for single-column readability."),
